# --- build output ---
build/
*/build/
.gradle/
*/.gradle/
build.log
run.txt
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# --- IDE ---
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
out/
.kotlin/
.vscode/

# --- server runtime: never commit these ---
# Credentials. auth.enc/auth.key authenticate the server to Hytale's session
# service; treat them like passwords.
auth.enc
auth.key
*.pem
.env

# Player data. spellshot/users.json is the progression store (levels, stats,
# saved loadouts); universe/players holds Hytale's own per-player saves.
#
# Both names are listed. The directory was called everlands/ before the rename,
# and UserStore migrates it on first boot -- but a server that has not booted
# since, or a backup taken before it did, still has the old name. Ignoring only
# the new one would quietly start committing player data on those.
#
# The `**/` prefixes matter. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so a bare `universe/players/` here only ever
# matched a universe/ at the repo root -- it did NOT cover
# lobby/server/universe/players/ or moshpit/server/universe/players/. Those only
# stayed out because one had its own .gitignore and the other happened to be
# empty. Now that the worlds are committed, these have to match at any depth.
# The progression store, written next to the server jar at runtime.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and scoped to the server directories. It was
# once a bare `everlands/`, which matches at ANY depth -- and since every source
# file lives under `net/everlands/`, that one line silently excluded the entire
# Kotlin codebase from the repository. 161 source files, no warning, and a
# published repo that built nothing.
/spellshot/
*/server/spellshot/
/everlands/
*/server/everlands/
**/universe/players/
**/universe/memories*
users.json*

# Server-local config and moderation lists
bans.json
whitelist.json
permissions.json
logs/
.cache/
backups/
updater/

# --- world data ---
# Both worlds ship in EXTRACTED form (moshpit/server/universe/ and
# lobby/server/universe/); the archives they came from do not. See the note in
# README on the arenas -- they are recreations of maps from other games and are
# not covered by this project's licence.
*.zip
!*/src/**/*.zip

# The moshpit arena world IS published, in extracted form under
# moshpit/server/universe/. The zip it came from is not: committing both would
# double 55 MB for nothing, and the zip additionally contains the 8,451 player
# save files from the original Everlands server. The extracted copy deliberately
# omits those -- the `universe/players/` and `universe/memories*` rules above
# keep them out even if someone re-extracts the archive in place.
moshpit/server/universe.zip

# lobby-universe/ is just an extraction of lobby-universe.zip; the canonical
# copy is lobby/server/universe/. Committing both doubles 8 MB for nothing.
lobby/lobby-universe/

# Scratch server created by run-local.ps1. Holds a copy of the world plus
# hardlinks to a 3.2 GB Assets.zip and the server jar. Disposable.
.local-test/

# Debris from recovering the arena markers after the registration bug wiped them.
# Kept on disk locally as a fallback, not worth publishing.
*.wiped
*.with-old-nuketown

# Export of the arena markers, for /arena import. Regenerate by copying
# moshpit/server/universe/worlds/Moshpit/resources/MiniGameArenaResource.json here.
/arena-markers.json
